  "notes": "Mainly describes the behavior of children who are in a bad mood, whining and crying or being demanding.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ぐずり{始|はじ}める: to start fussing\n- ぐずって⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧: to be fussing\n\nUSAGE: Most commonly used about babies and small children. The related adverb ⟦ぐずぐず→ぐずぐず：05844_guzuguzu⟧ describes being slow or indecisive.",
